# The WIDE refusal capture, deliberately shot and deliberately never kept.
# film-capture.mjs re-shoots c07b-refusal on every run, so it reappears as an
# untracked file each time; its own `what` note says the frame's lower half is
# the CASL block showing the shipped placeholder "123 Example Ave NW, Edmonton,
# AB T5A 0A1" and directs the film to c07b-refusal-statement instead, which
# carries a mustNotContain guard against exactly that text. Nothing here is real
# client data (mailingAddress is NULL) — the point is that address-shaped text
# must not reach the film, and the -statement- pair is what ships. Only these
# two names: the -statement- captures ARE tracked and must stay so.
creative/nevamis/captures/c07b-refusal-16x9.png
creative/nevamis/captures/c07b-refusal-9x16.png

# Credentials. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC — it is served by GitHub Pages at
# nevamis.ca. It had no .env rule at all until 2026-08-06, while shipping an
# .env.example that names TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN, ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, CALCOM_API_KEY
# and STRIPE_SECRET_KEY. Nothing was leaked, but the only thing standing
# between a local .env and worldwide publication was remembering not to type
# "git add -A" — and the rule three lines above this one exists because
# somebody already typed it once.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
